<title>USA: Enron buys wind power firm, sets new unit.</title>
<headline>Enron buys wind power firm, sets new unit.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enron Corp, based in Houston, Texas, announced Monday it has acquired Zond Corp, a wind power developer based in Tehachapi, Calif.</p>
<p>The purchase price was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Enron also said it plans to form a new business unit to pursue renewable energy resources.</p>
<p>Robert Kelly was named chairman and chief executive officer of the new unit, Enron Renewable Energy Corp. He was also appointed as a member of Enron's management committee.</p>
<p>Zond has installed and operates over 2,400 wind turbines comprising 260 megawatts.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
